    "certainty": "C",
    "source": "A1",
    "note": "Conservative swept bounds X [-1.25,1.25], Y [0,2.55], Z [-2,1.2]. Exact maximum barrel radial sweep about X is sqrt((0.595+0.035)^2+0.45^2)=0.774209274 m. It reaches world Y [0.685790726,2.234209274], leaving 0.005790726 m above chassis. Moving X extent is [-1.17,1.17]. Wheel bottom is Y=0, trails reach Z=-2."
  },
  "frame": {
    "handedness": "right",
    "up": "+Y",
    "forward": "+Z",
    "origin": "Ground below centre of assembly. Local part transforms are relative to parent."
  },
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "id": "A0",
      "statement": "No historical scale or performance is inferred from a modern replica.",
      "reason": "The sheet and museum models are distinct evidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "statement": "All dimensions and XYZ placements in parts are original exhibit choices in metres. Barrel spacing 0.15, barrel length 0.90, solid radius 0.035, eleven per bank, three banks 120 degrees apart. Frame width 1.8, wheel radius 0.50. Trail centre height 0.50 gives 0.055 vertical overlap with chassis. Shaft radius 0.055, length 2.34, world centre [0,1.46,0]. Endplate X intervals [-0.845,-0.795] and [0.795,0.845] leave 0.035 clearance to the uprights. Upright bore is a clockwise 32-sided polygon with circumradius 0.056 and centre [0,0.36,0] in each upright frame. Every remaining part dimension and transform is explicitly listed in its A1-tagged part. These are not measured historic calibres or dimensions.",
      "reason": "The image identifies topology and counts, not a metric shop drawing."
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "statement": "Manual indexing through 120 degrees takes 12 s, with 6 s rest before each index, repeated three times. Smoothstep gives maximum angular rate 0.2617993878 rad/s. This is an interpretive turning speed, not a documented gun rate. One shaft turn is a 1:1 handbar turn.",
      "reason": "No historical gearing or timing specified. Index directly by hand on the shaft, no invented speed multiplication."
    }
  ],
